# Running a docker-compose.yml needs two things, and the `docker` package is
# not one of them:
#
#   podman          the engine, and the API socket it serves
#   docker-compose  the Compose implementation. A standalone Go binary with no
#                   dependencies; it speaks the Docker API over $DOCKER_HOST.
#                   Podman's socket implements that API, so Compose cannot tell
#                   the difference — verified by running a real project against
#                   it with no Docker daemon present.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed:
#
#   docker          only needed if you want to toggle to a real Docker daemon,
#                   or to use `docker compose` (with a space) — that form is the
#                   docker CLI invoking a plugin, so it needs this package.
#                   `docker-compose` (hyphenated) works standalone.
#   docker-buildx   BuildKit, which podman's API emulation does not serve. The
#                   podman engine file sets DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0 for that reason,
#                   so buildx only earns its keep on the real-Docker side.
#   podman-compose  an independent Python reimplementation that shells out to
#                   the podman CLI rather than using the API. It groups services
#                   into a pod, so they share a network namespace and reach each
#                   other on localhost instead of by service name — compose files
#                   can behave differently under it. docker-compose is the
#                   reference implementation; prefer it.

podman
docker-compose
